{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013423-eternally-human","id":1013423,"title":"Eternally Human","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-06T15:23:45-08:00","id":1013423,"title":"Eternally Human","content":"I have noticed that pretty much every splat is about people becoming something else with the exception of HtV (usually) or vice versa (monsters becoming human). What about a mortal striving to reinforce his/her humanity and saying &quot;My humanity is enough.&quot; What would they go through to remain normally human, to keep out the corruption of the darkness, to remain human in life and death, and from now into eternity. I am aware of that the core book is Mortals and HtV is pretty much Mortals Go to War, but fighting the darkness is not the same as staying purely human indefinitely. So what do you guys think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7106-extant-reality","name":"Extant Reality","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7106_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T15:48:55-08:00","id":1013449,"title":"","content":"That is a very excellent point,<br /> <br /> I would imagine there are some Mystery Cuts and maybe even Conspiracies out there dedicated to the purity of Humaniy against forces of corruption. This is the Chronicles or Darkness though, so the price of remaining human in life and death would come at a terrible price for those in such an organization, but they might also come with some neat powers too. Like Temenos themed Supernatural Merits that reinforce the human aspects of monsters to level the playing field when creatures of the night come to feed off their loved ones. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Polish 12-06-2016, 06:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T15:57:04-08:00","id":1013450,"title":"","content":"I don't perceive it as &quot;trying to stay human&quot;, although some sort of do align that way. But by and large, it's more &quot;These people around me are still people, and even if I have to prey on them for reasons, I belong in this society with them, so I should be mindful of that and keep in touch with it to keep anchored in society, particularly since I more often then not came from them and know their pains and problems in a way unlike a wolf eating a rabbit.&quot;<br /> <br /> Basically, being a monster is no excuse for being a jackass, even if you're eating people-especially if you're eating people.<br /> <br /> Like, that's the thing: in a non-governmental sense, monsters are still a part of society, and they can either contribute to it or be a detriment to it. This is the world we live in. The attempts to remember what humanity means for the humans as well as figuring out the monster's relationship to humanity even if they are no longer a part of it is to decide to play the part in that world, to be, well.<br /> <br /> Not an asshole.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T16:16:59-08:00","id":1013461,"title":"","content":"I mean, as you say, the hook of most of the published material for CofD is being a supernatural creature (or someone aware of such) who's hidden in the regular human world we all know.<br /> <br /> What do you have in mind with &quot;retaining your humanity?&quot; What would the character be doing? Are they still engaging with the supernatural world in some way? What's the difference between a character who actively seeks to &quot;retain their humanity&quot; and a character who lives a standard human life (for all the definitions of standard human life) without ever encountering something a real-world person wouldn't encounter?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T16:30:59-08:00","id":1013471,"title":"","content":"I don't really understand how this could ever work as a gameline.<br /> <br /> Accountant: the Filing doesn't exactly gel with the themes of the setting, y'know?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T16:45:58-08:00","id":1013480,"title":"","content":"Also, in terms of the question as a game, welcome to Hunter the Vigil.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T16:58:35-08:00","id":1013485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013423-eternally-human?p=1013471#post1013471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't really understand how this could ever work as a gameline.<br /> <br /> Accountant: the Filing doesn't exactly gel with the themes of the setting, y'know?</div> </div> </div> </div>Work through tax season, then tell me you still think that it wouldn't fit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T18:14:52-08:00","id":1013507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Extant Reality</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013423-eternally-human#post1013423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would they go through to remain normally human, to keep out the corruption of the darkness, to remain human in life and death, and from now into eternity. I am aware of that the core book is Mortals and HtV is pretty much Mortals Go to War, but fighting the darkness is not the same as staying purely human indefinitely. So what do you guys think?</div> </div> </div> </div>'Keeping out the corruption of the darkness' is fighting it.<br /> <br /> But the darkness in Chronicles of Darkness is not some pervasive evil, it's not even a corrupting force, it's just mystery. And humans love mystery.<br /> <br /> One can delve headlong into occultism and become a leader of a cult that sacrifices people to Mammon in exchange for stock tips and still be fully, purely human.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T18:43:04-08:00","id":1013517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013423-eternally-human?p=1013507#post1013507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 'Keeping out the corruption of the darkness' is fighting it.<br /> <br /> But the darkness in Chronicles of Darkness is not some pervasive evil, it's not even a corrupting force, it's just mystery. And humans love mystery.<br /> <br /> One can delve headlong into occultism and become a leader of a cult that sacrifices people to Mammon in exchange for stock tips and still be fully, purely human.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless they're not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T19:23:21-08:00","id":1013538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013423-eternally-human?p=1013507#post1013507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 'Keeping out the corruption of the darkness' is fighting it.<br /> <br /> But the darkness in Chronicles of Darkness is not some pervasive evil, it's not even a corrupting force, it's just mystery. And humans love mystery.<br /> <br /> One can delve headlong into occultism and become a leader of a cult that sacrifices people to Mammon in exchange for stock tips and still be fully, purely human.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is one of my favorite themes to play with in game - every major supernatural (including some Hunters) is plugged into some otherworldly force that if it doesn't make living a normal human life impossibly, it certainly keeps it from being easy.<br /> <br /> But the Mammon Cultist? He could have been anyone or done so many other things. Instead, he decided he liked money and power, and if sacrificing some bums,illegals, or hippies is what is needed to get it, then it <i>sucks to be them</i>. Our world doesn't have real werewolves, or mages, or vampires or any of those things - but it is ~full~ of people like the Mammon Cultist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T05:30:35-08:00","id":1013697,"title":"","content":"Quite a few of the lines also posit that humanity is already deeply compromised by the supernatural. Humanity seems to have been deeply integrated into the systems of the God-Machine, the Shadow impacts people on a massive scale and the Abyss/quiescence is present in almost all of humanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T09:54:18-08:00","id":1013808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013423-eternally-human?p=1013507#post1013507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But the darkness in Chronicles of Darkness is not some pervasive evil, it's not even a corrupting force, it's just mystery. And humans love mystery.<br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>In that case, I would imagine someone trying to remain fully human would be someone trying to make sure no-one looks into the mysteries. Trying to make sure no-one learns about the supernatural and thus can be corrupted by it. In which case, what you are playing is an agent of the conspiracy that shores up the masquerade; Which, who knows, may be interesting. Probably better then Accountant the Filing at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T10:49:54-08:00","id":1013837,"title":"","content":"I can think of some ways for such material to work, but not as a standalone game line. Maybe a blue book approaching the theme for other games.<br /> <br /> There is the extremist, for Hunter, the Vigil. Some people take &quot;purity&quot; to another level, and it isn't pretty when those people become aware of the Darkness. Imagine someone who comes across all the good the supernatural can also carry, but still goes ahead with the hate of a nazi for Jews and Roma.<br /> <br /> Among every monster's splat, there could be the people who focus on actually being people. Not a simple Ghost Wolf who denies its condition, but an actual Tribe or Lodge that defends you still being human, even under such condition. A Covenant that teaches its members that being undead doesn't makes you above law (self-defense and necessity can be used to justify feeding as needed). And so on. I missed something in those lines, indeed, and my personal best werewolf character would easily turn to such a society as soon as she finds about it.<br /> <br /> You could also, of course, have the splat's group for &quot;curing the curse&quot;. The Ordo Dracul wants to transcend the vampire to something beyond life and undeath, but what about people who just want to become mortals again? And what if they not only want to turn back to human, but to actually turn or destroy all their fellow monsters? Some crossover with Hunter could be done with a society of monsters that are sworn to fight their own kind, in a way player-friendly, instead of the mysterious and inaccessible VII (no, I'm not against VII, I like it).<br /> <br /> Finally, some Hunters could be devoted to help such monsters, or at least have similar goals, either trying to apply human law to offending supernaturals, or trying to find a &quot;cure&quot; for their state.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T11:25:58-08:00","id":1013861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Urbenmyth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013423-eternally-human?p=1013808#post1013808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In that case, I would imagine someone trying to remain fully human would be someone trying to make sure no-one looks into the mysteries. Trying to make sure no-one learns about the supernatural and thus can be corrupted by it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Part of my point was that while being ignorant is part of the human condition, so is being curious. Also that the supernatural, as is, isn't a corruptive force any more than air and lemons are. It exists, acknowledging it doesn't make one corrupted, even embracing it doesn't corrupt you any more than you're corrupt for using a computer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013423-eternally-human?p=1013837#post1013837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Among every monster's splat, there could be the people who focus on actually being people. Not a simple Ghost Wolf who denies its condition, but an actual Tribe or Lodge that defends you still being human, even under such condition. A Covenant that teaches its members that being undead doesn't makes you above law (self-defense and necessity can be used to justify feeding as needed). And so on. I missed something in those lines, indeed, and my personal best werewolf character would easily turn to such a society as soon as she finds about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is something else, however. While there are vampire covenants that embrace humanity, like the Sun-Walking Knights and Carthians, werewolves flat out aren't human. Trying to be human is just going to lead to you raging uncontrollably for sometimes hours at a time.<br /> <br /> Something perhaps more fitting for this is Demon, which the OP left out. A demon isn't human, a demon wasn't human, but a demon can appreciate that humans are everywhere and perhaps they have something going for them, and seek to be human.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-07-2016, 02:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T00:10:55-08:00","id":1014200,"title":"","content":"The fundamental question here is, what it means to be &quot;Human&quot;? It is a quite abstract exercise. A werewolf isn't Human in a direct sense, but they are people in another sense. A character that denies the nature of the werewolf as a hunter and a spirit-thing is in it for some nasty consequences. But that is what means to be Human? Maybe some of those poor bastards think so. But some can have another definition for it altogether. I'm not saying that they teach you should forget your condition and try to stay in human form the rest of your life. But what about teaching that you are still able to feel like a human, to think like a human, and to live in society like a human, and though you have other abilities and special necessities, they don't justify you not respecting human society or law.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T00:58:38-08:00","id":1014204,"title":"","content":"Isn't this basically Deviant? In Deviant, your humanity is compromised, and you're trying to avoid making it worse by living your life and living with the changes made to it. To become stronger is to become less human, something that in general you really don't want.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T12:34:08-08:00","id":1014414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Extant Reality</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013423-eternally-human#post1013423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have noticed that pretty much every splat is about people becoming something else with the exception of HtV (usually) or vice versa (monsters becoming human). What about a mortal striving to reinforce his/her humanity and saying &quot;My humanity is enough.&quot; What would they go through to remain normally human, to keep out the corruption of the darkness, to remain human in life and death, and from now into eternity. I am aware of that the core book is Mortals and HtV is pretty much Mortals Go to War, but fighting the darkness is not the same as staying purely human indefinitely. So what do you guys think?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is too undefined. What's &quot;corruption&quot;? What's &quot;darkness&quot;? How do they prevent themselves from being changed by mere <i>exposure</i> to impurity? Do they do it through studied ignorance? (Or would that be inhuman?) Do they do it by ritual cleansing? (Or would that be inhuman?)<br /> <br /> What does it mean to fight against something without going to (a metaphorical) war? How is that accomplished? What choices do they face? What tradeoffs do they make? What options are denied to them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T06:12:48-08:00","id":1014724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013423-eternally-human?p=1013837#post1013837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could also, of course, have the splat's group for &quot;curing the curse&quot;. The Ordo Dracul wants to transcend the vampire to something beyond life and undeath, but what about people who just want to become mortals again? And what if they not only want to turn back to human, but to actually turn or destroy all their fellow monsters? Some crossover with Hunter could be done with a society of monsters that are sworn to fight their own kind, in a way player-friendly, instead of the mysterious and inaccessible VII (no, I'm not against VII, I like it).</div> </div> </div> </div>I want just point to fresh forum made <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1013859-2e-lodge-of-the-curse?p=1014317#post1014317\">Lodge of Curse</a> for <b>Werewolf 2E </b>about this very thing. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013423-eternally-human?p=1014200#post1014200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fundamental question here is, what it means to be &quot;Human&quot;? It is a quite abstract exercise. A werewolf isn't Human in a direct sense, but they are people in another sense. A character that denies the nature of the werewolf as a hunter and a spirit-thing is in it for some nasty consequences. But that is what means to be Human? Maybe some of those poor bastards think so. But some can have another definition for it altogether. I'm not saying that they teach you should forget your condition and try to stay in human form the rest of your life. But what about teaching that you are still able to feel like a human, to think like a human, and to live in society like a human, and though you have other abilities and special necessities, they don't justify you not respecting human society or law.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is not this whole shtick of Iron Masters in <b>Werewolf</b>? This Tribe is all about adaptation to human society, they are obsessed with humans and have highest rankings of werewolves dedicated to human culture. They motto is to literally blend with humans. 'Wolf in sheep clothing' and all that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T11:15:04-08:00","id":1014847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013423-eternally-human?p=1014724#post1014724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want just point to fresh forum made <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1013859-2e-lodge-of-the-curse?p=1014317#post1014317\">Lodge of Curse</a> for <b>Werewolf 2E </b>about this very thing. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Is not this whole shtick of Iron Masters in <b>Werewolf</b>? This Tribe is all about adaptation to human society, they are obsessed with humans and have highest rankings of werewolves dedicated to human culture. They motto is to literally blend with humans. 'Wolf in sheep clothing' and all that.</div> </div> </div> </div>That Lodge is cool. I would tweak it a little, but overall good.<br /> <br /> About the Iron Master there is an important twist in there, though I would expect most adherents of a Lodge dedicated to being human to be Iron Masters (my character that was like that, though, was a Bone Shadow). But you see, &quot;Wolf in Sheep's Clothes&quot; is far different than &quot;Wolf and Sheep are Both People&quot;. The Iron Masters blend among humanity with ease, tend to accompany more the development of human society. But they also choose humanity for the Siskur Dah. It isn't a sense of belonging, but of blending. One do not have to negate the other, but isn't the same thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}